=====================================================================
lisptc — a language showcase .ptc

Run me:
  pnpm --filter @lisptc/interpreter exec \
    node --experimental-transform-types src/lisp.ts ../../test.ptc

the interpreter runs each non-"-" argv entry as a script file
=====================================================================
(echo "=== 1. atoms, arithmetic & big numbers ===")

numbers are number | bigint; arithmetic promotes automatically
(echo (+ 1 2 3 4 5))
=> 15
(echo (* 6 7))
=> 42
(echo (/ 22 7))
=> rational-ish float
(echo (- 10 3 2))
=> 5
there is no expt in the prelude, so define one — the result is an exact bigint
(defun expt (base n) (if (= n 0) 1 (* base (expt base (- n 1)))))
(echo (expt 2 100))
=> 1267650600228229401496703205376, exact
(echo (< 1 2))
chained comparison via prelude
(echo "=== 2. lists & cons cells ===")

(setq xs (list 1 2 3 4 5))
(echo xs)
(echo (car xs))
=> 1
(echo (cdr xs))
=> 2 3 4 5
(echo (cadr xs))

=> 2
(echo (append xs (list 6 7)))
=> 1 .. 7
(echo (nreverse (list 1 2 3)))
=> 3 2 1
(echo "=== 3. lambdas, closures & higher order ===")

a closure capturing `n`
(defun adder (n) (lambda (x) (+ x n)))
(setq add10 (adder 10))
(echo (add10 5))
=> 15
(echo (mapcar add10 (list 1 2 3)))
=> 11 12 13
fold via recursion
(defun reduce (f acc lst) (if (null lst) acc
    (reduce f (f acc (car lst)) (cdr lst))))
(echo (reduce + 0 (list 1 2 3 4 5)))
=> 15
(echo "=== 4. recursion ===")

(defun fact (n) (if (<= n 1) 1 (* n (fact (- n 1)))))
(echo (fact 20))
=> 2432902008176640000
(echo (fact 30))
=> big, exact bigint
(defun fib (n) (if (< n 2) n (+ (fib (- n 1)) (fib (- n 2)))))
(echo (fib 15))
=> 610
(echo "=== 5. control flow: cond / when / let / while / dolist ===")

(defun classify (n) (cond ((< n 0) 'negative) ((= n 0) 'zero) (t 'positive)))
(echo (mapcar classify (list -3 0 7)))

(let ((a 3) (b 4)) (echo (+ (* a a) (* b b))))
=> 25
imperative loop with mutation
(setq sum 0)
(dolist (x (list 10 20 30)) (setq sum (+ sum x)))
(echo sum)
=> 60
(setq i 0)
(setq acc nil)
(while (< i 5) (setq acc (cons i acc)) (setq i (+ i 1)))
(echo (nreverse acc))
=> 0 1 2 3 4
(echo "=== 6. macros & quasiquotation ===")

define our own control macro with `,` unquote and `,@` splice
(defmacro unless (test &rest body) `(cond ((not ,test) ,@body)))
(echo (unless nil 'ran 'ok))
=> ok
a macro that builds code at expansion time
(defmacro swap (a b) `(let ((tmp ,a)) (setq ,a ,b) (setq ,b tmp)))
(setq p 1)
(setq q 2)
(swap p q)
(echo (list p q))
=> 2 1
(echo "=== 7. association lists (symbolic data) ===")

(setq db '((alice .30) (bob .25) (carol .35)))
(echo (assoc 'bob db))
=> bob . 25
(echo (cdr (assoc 'carol db)))
=> 35
(echo "=== 8. MCP support ===")

MCP built-ins are installed on every Interp:
  load-mcp / unload-mcp / list-mcps / list-tools
  search-tools / mcp-shutdown
Tool docs surface through the generic `doc` built-in.

Load a server ad-hoc. Here we boot the repo's fixture stdio server,
which exposes a single tool, `echo`.
(await (load-mcp :name "fs" :command "npx" :args '("-y" "@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem" "/tmp")))

(fs/read_file "/tmp/test")

What servers are loaded, and how many tools each has?
(list-mcps)
=> fx :loaded 1
Enumerate tools: symbol param-count doc
(list-tools "fs")

Full documentation for one tool, including per-parameter docs.
(doc 'fs/echo)

Fuzzy search across all loaded tools, ranked best-first.
(echo (search-tools "echo text back"))

Each tool is an ordinary global binding named <server>/<tool>,
called with native keyword syntax. The synchronous interpreter
blocks on the async broker under the hood.
(fs/echo :message "hello from lisptc")

=> "hello from lisptc"
Unload releases the tool bindings; shutdown tears down the broker.
(unload-mcp "fs")

=> fx/echo
(mcp-shutdown)

(echo "=== done ===")

(cddr '(1 4 5))

(cddr (4 (5 5)))

(echo)

(await (load-mcp "playwright"))
(await (load-mcp "linear"))
(playwright/browser_navigate :url "yourscrib.ai")

(search-tools "navigate")

(playwright/browser_navigate :url "hyko.ai")

(unload-mcp "playwright")

(await (load-mcp :name "linear" :url "https://mcp.linear.app/mcp" :headers (list (cons "Authorization" (concat "Bearer " (secret "LINEAR_API_KEY"))))))
(secrets)

(concat (secret "REPL_LINEAR_API_KEY") "--test")

(length (secret "REPL_LINEAR_API_KEY"))

(defmacro swap (a b) `(let ((tmp ,a)) (setq ,a ,b) (setq ,b tmp)))
(setq p 1)
(setq q 2)

(swap p q)
(list q p)
